    "id": "AAS_4296_10km_habitats_ufcm_1 ",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "These habitats were delineated using the following input variables: Degree days (-5 degrees), annual solar radiation, slope, elevation, ice melt and rugosity. These input variables were utilized in a unsupervised fuzzy c-mean classification to delineate 8 habitats on a 10km grid covering the entire ice-free area of the Antarctic continent.\n    \nThe shapefile provided is stored in a Polar Stereographic projection with true scale at 71 degrees south.\nThe numbers refer to the different habitats.",
